#: ../../source/docs/slung-payload.rst:5
#: 63160266e04c479c9a58651a658557aa
msgid "Slung Payload"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/slung-payload.rst:10
#: 4ee32de335c547eda0f4405aa6e8ea44
msgid "For package delivery using a slung payload can be simpler and more reliable than using a :ref:`winch <common-daiwa-winch>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/slung-payload.rst:12
#: 81a333cceb184232a8e4791350ef86f3
msgid "Copter-4.6 (and higher) supports the `copter-slung-payload.lua <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/libraries/AP_Scripting/applets/copter-slung-payload.lua>`__ script which can be used to reduce the oscillation of the payload"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/slung-payload.rst:15
#: f4602568046f43ff8412b1f3156e22ad
msgid "Hardware Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/slung-payload.rst:20
#: 5dcdbf5192084a2a8e98ec596c1aa31d
msgid "Mount an autopilot, GPS and telemetry radio to the payload.  This payload autopilot must transmit the `GLOBAL_POSITION_INT <https://mavlink.io/en/messages/common.html#GLOBAL_POSITION_INT>`__ mavlink message to the autopilot at 10hz using a system id that is different from the autopilot's.  In the video above a `Here4 GPS running ArduPilot <https://docs.cubepilot.org/user-guides/here-4/here-4-manual#id-8.-installing-ardupilot-on-here4>`__ was used along with an ESP32 radio running `DroneBridge ESP32 <https://github.com/DroneBridge/ESP32>`__.  A `ready-to-use device is available from Japan Drones <https://japandrones.com/shop/shopdetail.html?brandcode=000000000193>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/slung-payload.rst:21
#: 64badd35435940b0931fdc97b97694d8
msgid "The payload should be connected to the delivery vehicle with fishing line (or equivalent).  Both ends of the fishing line should have fishing tackle bearing swivels attached to allow the payload to rotate freely.  Two or three fishing sinkers should be attached at 0.5m intervals to the end of the line closest to the payload"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/slung-payload.rst:22
#: 52ce37ebefb048a19731eaa7f195060e
msgid "The fishing line should be wound around a fishing line coiling plate starting from the payload end"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/slung-payload.rst:23
#: e00ddcf16c314b40bf978876260409ce
msgid "The coiling plate should be attached to a heavy base board and placed directly under the delivery vehicle so that the line uncoils smoothly as the vehicle climbs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/slung-payload.rst:24
#: 1b0ac1408e52433ba51a0ed2118eb3f8
msgid "The delivery drone should have a :ref:`servo gripper <common-gripper-servo>` allowing it to release the entire line during the :ref:`payload place mission command <mission-command-list>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/slung-payload.rst:47
#: 60164be51d5d4a40b4cbc0efa27e14be
msgid "Software Configuration and Testing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/slung-payload.rst:49
#: dda94fee27c84d20951d80b4774a87c0
msgid "Install the `copter-slung-payload.lua <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/libraries/AP_Scripting/applets/copter-slung-payload.lua>`__ script onto the delivery vehicle's autopilot (see :ref:`Lua script installation instructions here <common-lua-scripts>`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/slung-payload.rst:50
#: a7a29c3e48ac49d190dd450e26dc7846
msgid "Follow the \"How To Use\" section of the `copter-slung-payload.md file <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/libraries/AP_Scripting/applets/copter-slung-payload.md>`__ including copying the `modules directory <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/tree/master/libraries/AP_Scripting/modules>`__ to the vehicle's autopilot's SD card's scripts directory"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/slung-payload.rst:51
#: b2f3a1dc5daf4d8a8d431ecb2a38cbbd
msgid "Power on the vehicle and the payload's autopilot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/slung-payload.rst:52
#: bcda6074b7874c6f8d85bdc7d5ff8d04
msgid "Connect to the vehicle's autopilot with a ground station (e.g. Mission Planner) and confirm that both the vehicle and payload appear on the map.  If they do not then there is likely an issue with the telemetry radios or the delivery vehicle and payload's  sysid conflict (see :ref:`MAV_SYSID <MAV_SYSID>`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/slung-payload.rst:53
#: 7312f2d638954edc9dafe93a5be8fddb
msgid "Create an auto mission with SCRIPT_TIME and/or PAYLOAD_PLACE :ref:`mission commands <mission-command-list>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/slung-payload.rst:54
#: a27c43221df84bea9f6eda0d042dcd8b
msgid "Fly the mission and confirm that the delivery vehicle's autopilot reports, \"copter-slung-payload: activated\" during the NAV_SCRIPT and/or PAYLOAD_PLACE mission commands.  Also confirm the vehicle moves slightly towards the payload when activated"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/slung-payload.rst:55
#: fe540c03069d483eb04c11f8a32732f8
msgid "If the delivery vehicle moves strangely, simply switch the vehicle to a different flight mode (e.g. Guide, RTL, etc) or advance the mission so that neither a NAV_SCRIPT nor PAYLOAD_PLACE command is executed"
msgstr ""

